{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:founder-d-reviewer-fable-05", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:3a7765ac1f2d5c06b5c6", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "issue_class": "issue-class:complemented-panel-for-supplied-panel-emission", "bounded_statement": "In this workflow the emission-weighted comparison was computed against the complement (1 - panel_leak_call) of the supplied reference-panel values rather than against the panel values in their supplied coding, while the report claims the comparison was made in the supplied coding. Consequently the reported per-unit agreement rate (0.2000) and confirmed emission inventory (934 kg/day) are the complement-coding results; the supplied-coding results would be 20/25 = 0.8000 and 9142 kg/day. The report is also internally inconsistent: it states 20 of 25 units agree yet reports an agreement rate of 0.2000.", "root_cause": "workflow/analysis.py constructs panel_reference_values = [PANEL_BASELINE - value for value in panel_calls] (line 37) and feeds those complemented values into agreement_selector (line 39); the resulting selectors drive both the reported agreement_rate (line 42) and the emission_terms accumulation (lines 43-44). The report text nonetheless asserts comparison 'in the coding in which the reference panel is supplied' and displays staged_agreement_units = total_units - concordant_units (the supplied-coding count, 20) alongside the complement-coding rate 0.2000 and complement-coding emission 934, masking the substitution.", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The workflow complements every supplied panel value before any comparison; PANEL_BASELINE is 1, so this is 1 - panel_call for each unit.", "observed_value": "panel_reference_values holds the bitwise complement of panel_calls", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 9, "end_line": 9, "quoted_text": "PANEL_BASELINE = 1"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 37, "end_line": 37, "quoted_text": "panel_reference_values = [PANEL_BASELINE - value for value in panel_calls]"}]}, {"description": "The agreement selectors that drive both the reported agreement rate and the emission accumulation are computed against the complemented values, not the supplied panel_calls.", "observed_value": "selectors compare observed_calls to panel_reference_values (the complement)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 39, "end_line": 39, "quoted_text": "selectors = [agreement_selector(observed_calls[index], panel_reference_values[index]) for index in range(total_units)]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 42, "end_line": 43, "quoted_text": "agreement_rate = concordant_units / total_units\nemission_terms = [daily_rates[index] * selectors[index] for index in range(total_units)]"}]}, {"description": "The reported emission-accumulation agreement rate 0.2000 equals 5/25, the count of units where observed_leak_call equals 1 - panel_leak_call (WP-04, WP-07, WP-13, WP-19, WP-24); the supplied-coding rate is 20/25 = 0.8000.", "observed_value": "0.2000", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "- Per-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.2000"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "WP-04,Permian,2025-Q2,95,1,0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "WP-07,Anadarko,2025-Q2,176,0,1"}]}, {"description": "The accumulated emission 934 kg/day equals the sum of measured_kg_per_day over exactly the five complement-coding-concordant pads (95+176+358+118+187 = 934), not the twenty supplied-coding-concordant pads (which sum to 9142).", "observed_value": "934", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "- Accumulated confirmed emission value: 934 kg per day"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "WP-13,Denver-Julesburg,2025-Q2,358,1,0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 20, "quoted_text": "WP-19,Uinta,2025-Q2,118,0,1"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "WP-24,Bakken,2025-Q2,187,1,0"}]}, {"description": "The report explicitly claims the comparison was performed in the supplied coding and that no method deviation exists, contradicting the complement substitution visible in the code.", "observed_value": "false supplied-coding claim", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 9, "quoted_text": "for each pad with a single equality selector, in the coding in which the reference\npanel is supplied."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 28, "end_line": 28, "quoted_text": "No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Against my verdict: the report's line 'Units whose observed call equals the reference-panel call: 20' matches the correct supplied-coding agreement count, suggesting some supplied-coding computation was performed. However, tracing the code shows this figure is staged_agreement_units = total_units - concordant_units, a derived display value; the rate (0.2000) and emission (934) actually used by the accumulation come from the complemented comparison, and 20/25 is arithmetically inconsistent with the reported rate 0.2000, so this line does not rescue the report.", "observed_value": "20 (display-only figure inconsistent with reported rate)", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "- Units whose observed call equals the reference-panel call: 20"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 41, "end_line": 41, "quoted_text": "staged_agreement_units = total_units - concordant_units"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the verdict three ways. (1) I checked whether PANEL_BASELINE - value could be an identity or legitimate re-coding: PANEL_BASELINE is 1 and panel values are 0/1, so it is strictly the complement, and no protocol amendment authorizes a re-coding (the report itself denies any deviation). (2) I independently recomputed both codings from inputs/data.csv: supplied coding gives 20/25 agreement (rate 0.8000) and a selected emission of 9142 kg/day; complement coding gives 5/25 (rate 0.2000) and 934 kg/day. The reported rate and emission match the complement coding exactly, ruling out coincidence. (3) I checked whether the reported '20 of 25 in agreement' could indicate the emission used supplied coding: it cannot, because the emission terms are built from the same complement-based selectors, and 934 is reproducible only from the five complement-concordant pads. All three attempts failed to overturn the verdict.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:769d1c65c50fd5c323ac", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "issue_class": null, "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The emission accumulation multiplies emission_factor(observed, panel_calls[index]) over all units, using the panel values in their supplied coding; complement_calls never enters this loop.", "observed_value": "emission accumulation uses panel_calls (supplied coding)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 32, "end_line": 32, "quoted_text": "panel_calls = [int(record[\"panel_call\"]) for record in rows]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 53, "end_line": 54, "quoted_text": "for index in range(unit_count):\n    emission_value = emission_value * emission_factor(observed_calls[index], panel_calls[index])"}]}, {"description": "The reported per-unit agreement rate is likewise computed from supplied-coding comparisons (agreement_flags against panel_calls), and independent recomputation from inputs/data.csv confirms 18/24 concordant units (mismatches at BAR-003, 006, 011, 014, 019, 022), rate 0.750000, and emission product (1/2)^6 = 1/64, all matching the report.", "observed_value": "18/24 = 0.750000; 1/64 = 0.015625", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 40, "end_line": 41, "quoted_text": "agreement_flags = [concordance_indicator(observed_calls[index], panel_calls[index]) for index in range(unit_count)]\nagreement_count = sum(agreement_flags)"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "Per-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.750000 (18/24)"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 26, "end_line": 26, "quoted_text": "Accumulated emission value (product over 24 units): 1/64 = 0.015625"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "BAR-003,Tel_Hadya,BOPA1_2371-1163,A03,0.994,1,0"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Against my verdict: the workflow does construct a complemented panel (complement_calls = 1 - panel_call), which is the exact ingredient of the in-scope issue class. However, tracing every use of complement_calls shows it feeds only flip_flags/flip_agreement_count, which appears solely in the QC line of the report (strand-flip QC count: 6); it does not touch agreement_flags, agreement_rate, or the emission product, and the report accurately discloses this scope.", "observed_value": "complement used only in QC count, not in emission accumulation", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 33, "end_line": 33, "quoted_text": "complement_calls = [1 - value for value in panel_calls]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 44, "end_line": 45, "quoted_text": "flip_flags = [concordance_indicator(observed_calls[index], complement_calls[index]) for index in range(unit_count)]\nflip_agreement_count = sum(flip_flags)"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 21, "quoted_text": "It feeds this quality-control line only and never enters the emission accumulation.\nUnits whose array_call equals the complemented panel_call (strand-flip QC count): 6"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I actively tried to demonstrate the issue is present, since a complemented panel is literally constructed in this workflow. I traced every reference to complement_calls and flip_flags: they terminate in the single QC report line and never reach agreement_flags, agreement_rate, or the emission_value loop, which reference panel_calls directly. I then recomputed the numbers both ways from the data: supplied coding gives 18/24 concordant, rate 0.750000, product (1/2)^6 = 1/64; complement coding would give 6/24, rate 0.250000, product (1/2)^18 = 1/262144. The report's rate, product, and log10 (-1.806180 = log10(1/64)) all match the supplied coding and none match the complement coding. I also verified the QC count of 6 equals the complement-coding concordance, consistent with its disclosed role. I could not construct a reading under which the complemented panel influenced the emission-weighted result.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:afec8de43f6550605f4f", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "issue_class": null, "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The selectors driving both the agreement rate and the emission accumulation compare observed_calls directly against panel_calls as read from the supplied panel column; no complement or re-coding of the panel exists anywhere in the workflow.", "observed_value": "supplied-coding comparison throughout", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 35, "end_line": 35, "quoted_text": "panel_calls = [int(record[\"panel_leak_call\"]) for record in rows]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 37, "end_line": 37, "quoted_text": "selectors = [agreement_selector(observed_calls[index], panel_calls[index]) for index in range(total_units)]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 39, "end_line": 41, "quoted_text": "agreement_rate = concordant_units / total_units\nemission_terms = [daily_rates[index] * selectors[index] for index in range(total_units)]\nconfirmed_emission = sum(emission_terms)"}]}, {"description": "Independent recomputation from inputs/data.csv in the supplied coding confirms every reported figure: 20 of 25 pads agree (mismatches at WP-04, 07, 13, 19, 24), rate 0.8000, selected emission 9142 kg/day (10076 gross minus the five mismatched pads' 934), matching the report exactly.", "observed_value": "20/25 = 0.8000; 9142 kg/day; gross 10076 kg/day", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "- Per-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.8000\n- Accumulated confirmed emission value: 9142 kg per day"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Confirmed methane emission inventory: 9142 kg per day, from 20 of 25 well pads in agreement (per-unit agreement rate 0.8000)."}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "WP-01,Permian,2025-Q2,412,1,1"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Against my verdict, I looked for any construction that could invert or re-code the panel before comparison (an arithmetic complement, a swapped column read, or a non-identity mapping inside agreement_selector). The selector is a pure equality indicator scaled between SELECTOR_MISMATCH = 0 and SELECTOR_MATCH = 1, so it cannot invert the panel, and panel_leak_call is read verbatim as an int. No complement expression exists in the file.", "observed_value": "agreement_selector is a plain equality indicator; no complement construction found", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 22, "quoted_text": "def agreement_selector(observed_value, panel_value):\n    indicator = int(observed_value == panel_value)\n    weighted = SELECTOR_MISMATCH + (SELECTOR_MATCH - SELECTOR_MISMATCH) * indicator\n    return weighted"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 7, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "SELECTOR_MATCH = 1\nSELECTOR_MISMATCH = 0"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to demonstrate the in-scope issue by (1) searching the workflow for any complement, subtraction from a baseline, column swap, or re-coding of panel_leak_call before comparison — none exists; the panel column is parsed as int and passed unmodified into an equality-indicator selector; (2) recomputing the outputs under the hypothetical complement coding to see whether the report might secretly match it: complement coding would yield 5/25 agreement, rate 0.2000, and emission 934 kg/day, none of which appear in this report; and (3) verifying the reported figures (20/25, 0.8000, 9142, gross 10076) against my own supplied-coding recomputation from the data, which matched exactly. All attempts to find the issue failed, so the no-issue verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}